      "statement": "scripts/palette-check.py audits a web-capture PNG against rendered pixels to catch the global.css Uniwind variables drifting from theme.ts (or a capture taken in the wrong theme): it keeps a TOKENS table duplicated from theme.ts (comment says keep in sync), matches pixels within a per-channel tolerance of 8, auto-detects the theme by scoring which token set covers more sampled pixels (failing below 20% coverage unless --theme is passed), and reports per-token coverage while noting a legitimately unrendered token is not necessarily drift.",
